/*****************************************************************************
    firstLight is A4's form, on paper: the smallest form worth drawing, cut down
    from IncantForms/Windows/simple. Nothing draws it yet. See the notes below bail().
*****************************************************************************/
registry(fILEs);
define
    descriptionsFile File='IncantForms/Windows/descriptions';
    ;
include(descriptionsFile);
register(FORMs);
define
    insideForm;
    ;
insideForm := descriptions;
define
    okNote window x=0 y=0 width=400 height=200 down fill:=white font:=normalFont color:=blue
        okNoteText="You clicked OK. Click it again and the descriptions form comes back." text align=center valign=center;
    ;
define
    insideShown = 0;
    okClick code={
        ocWas = insideShown;
        if ocWas == 0;      insideForm := okNote;
        if ocWas == 0;      insideShown = 1;
        if ocWas == 1;      insideForm := descriptions;
        if ocWas == 1;      insideShown = 0;
        };
    ;
define
    firstLight window x=300 y=450 width=400 height=400 down fill:=wall font:=normalFont color:=blue
        heading="First Light" text height=43 font:=titleFont color:=green align=center bottomBorder;
        words="This text is poured into its frame. It should wrap at the frame's width and stop at the frame's height, and the form should report how much of it fit.\n\nA second paragraph holds {emphasis: one run} in a style of its own." text fill:=white align=justify;
        bar across height=35
            space;
            ok="OK" text width=60 border strokeColor:=red fill:=lightGreen align=center valign=center onClick:=okClick;
        inside form:=insideForm height=50%;
    ;
bail();

A FORM INSIDE A FIELD (G2 stroke 1b; Tony, 2026-11-13). inside holds the descriptions form: form:=descriptions. Layout gives
inside its frame (the lower half: height=50%), then lays descriptions out in that frame, and the draw walk draws it there.
firstLight grew from 400x200 to 400x400 so that heading, words and bar keep the frames they had; inside sits below bar.
This file includes IncantForms/Windows/descriptions itself, since a := names a field that must already be defined.
A form that holds itself is refused by name at layout (setFrame) and its field is left empty.
THE SWAP (G2 stroke 2; Tony, 2026-11-13). inside names insideForm, a field of its own outside the form that holds the form to
show: insideForm := descriptions. Writing it (insideForm := anotherForm) is one write, and it tells insideForm's listeners; a
listener that calls redrawForm shows the other form in the field. firstLight's own definition is never written by a swap.
THE CLICK (G2 stroke 3, the mock click; Tony, 2026-11-13). ok holds onClick:=okClick. okClick writes insideForm: the first
click shows okNote in the field, the next brings descriptions back. A click is click(request) in incant/utilities, the
request naming form:=firstLight and field="ok"; the redraw comes from insideForm's listener, not from the click.

Spelled to the forms plan's rulings. Style attributes sit on fields and are scoped to the subtree: font=normal holds for
everything under firstLight, and heading overrides it by naming font=title. fill is not inherited, so each field names its
own. bottomBorder is the ruled side spelling (Tony, 2026-11-04); the plan's A4 section carries the count and the walk.

Cut from simple, and why:
    onLayout code={}   event firing comes after A4
    text=one           one field showing another field's text is a field reference; the listener's family, parked
    two                a red block holding nothing
    pad                dropped by ruling (Tony, 2026-11-04)
    three, stuff, wrap the nesting that existed to carry text=one
    width=50.0%        the % is parsed as a Modifier and the width reads 50; a percentage needs its own spelling
    rounded            a border is enough for first light; rounded waits for the drawing step
    the name simple    UnitTests already has a field named simple, and the define merged into it

Added: down, a text field that pours, and a field shaped like A4's button. Nothing fires. It is plain text with a border
until event firing comes through it. The word button stays out because nothing reads it (formsTable).

Read it with IncantForms/WorkingOn/firstLightRead.

